{"id": "sevt_01KoVtYsEY8NVqctcjgRx345", "content": [{"text": "I created one ticket draft for the finding. It's marked **not exploitable**: the flagged SQL is built only from hardcoded test data, so an attacker has no way to affect it.\n\n| ID | Rule | Location | Verdict | Severity | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F-105 | SQL Injection | tests/fixtures/seed_db.py:10 | not_exploitable | none | The query is built by string concatenation, but the values come from a fixed list of test users (tests/fixtures/seed_db.py:3). The function's only input, the database file path, is used to open the database, not to build SQL. Nothing in the repo calls `seed()`. The only app route is `/health` (app/main.py:6-8), which returns a fixed response. |\n\n**Suggested cleanup (not a security fix):** switch to a parameterized query, `conn.executemany(\"INSERT INTO users VALUES (?, ?)\", USERS)`, so the pattern doesn't get copied into production code. You could also stop the scanner from treating `tests/` as production code.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-26T20:54:18.905131Z", "type": "agent.message"}
